Cyclo for Ubuntu and Debian
---------------------------

Cyclo is a host CLI. Installing this package does not start a daemon, create a
service account, add users to the docker group, or create Docker containers,
networks, or volumes.

Runtime prerequisites
---------------------

The package depends on Git, Docker Engine, and the separately packaged DComp
command. The invoking user must be able to access Docker and must not run Cyclo
as root. Confirm that DComp exposes machine API 1 before the first stateful
Cyclo command:

    dcomp version --json
    cyclo doctor

Configuration and credentials
-----------------------------

The packaged `/etc/cyclo/host.conf` is a comment-only example configuration.
The launcher defaults to `/var/lib/cyclo`, so its active host configuration is
`/var/lib/cyclo/host.conf`; leaving that file absent routes teams directly to
Cyclo's credential gateway. Put only provider-component declarations in host
configuration files. Do not put API keys or OAuth tokens in them.

The packaged `/usr/bin/cyclo` launcher defaults `CYCLO_STATE_ROOT` to
`/var/lib/cyclo`. That directory and the state files beneath it are world
readable and writable for this temporary global-state deployment model. This is
intentionally unsafe on a multi-user system: any local user can inspect or
modify Cyclo state. Set `CYCLO_STATE_ROOT` or use `--state-root` to choose an
independent state root instead.

Provider credentials remain in Cyclo's Docker volume, not in `/var/lib/cyclo`.
With the launcher default, host configuration is read from
`/var/lib/cyclo/host.conf`; an explicit alternative state root likewise uses
its own `host.conf`.
